

1. Student Marks Analyzer
Problem Statement

You are given an array of student objects containing their names and marks. Use higher-order functions to:

Find students who scored 80 or above.
Create a new array containing only their names.
Calculate the average marks of all students.

const students = [
  { name: "Rohan", marks: 85 },
  { name: "Priya", marks: 92 },
  { name: "Amit", marks: 68 },
  { name: "Sneha", marks: 78 },
  { name: "Ankit", marks: 88 }
];

const toppers = students.filter(student => student.marks >= 80);

const topperNames = toppers.map(student => student.name);

const averageMarks =
  students.reduce((sum, student) => sum + student.marks, 0) /
  students.length;

console.log("Toppers:", toppers);
console.log("Topper Names:", topperNames);
console.log("Average Marks:", averageMarks.toFixed(2));
